# sqlx hashes each migration file exactly as it sits in the working tree, and
# stores that sha384 in `_sqlx_migrations`. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF, which changes the hash and makes an
# already-migrated database abort startup with
# "migration N was previously applied but has been modified".
#
# The fork-authored migrations below were first applied with LF endings (they
# were written straight into the working tree, never checked out), so every
# checkout must reproduce LF or the resulting binary cannot open an existing
# CODEX_HOME. Upstream migrations are deliberately left alone: they were first
# applied from a CRLF checkout and must keep whatever the platform produces.
#
# Any new fork migration has to be pinned here too.
migrations/0053_thread_tombstones.sql text eol=lf
migrations/0056_thread_attachments.sql text eol=lf
workflow_migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
